/-!
# `Ct`: constant-time proofs for the Aeneas translation of the six-set crate (portable build)

The single-set tree's `lean/Ct` library (git `26aa3d8`) carried over to `rust/` (all six SHA-2
parameter sets). Files marked (link) are the single-set tree's file of the same name, unchanged
(they were symbolic links to it until the single-set tree was removed); (copy) are copies with
the changes their headers list; the others are this tree's own.

* `Ct/Leak.lean` (link) the leakage monad, events, `cond`, `loop`, erasure.
* `Ct/Do.lean` (link) `do` notation for `Leak`.
* `Ct/Model.lean` (link) the leakage model (trusted table).
* `Ct/ModelBuild.lean` this tree's part of the model: `core.slice.index.Slice.index_mut`
  (mutable sub-slices of slices), instrumented like `Slice.index`.
* `Ct/Funs.lean` GENERATED by `scripts/ct-gen.sh` from `Slhdsa/Funs.lean` (header only).
* `Ct/Check.lean` (copy) the checker; its whitelist has five more entries, marked `[six-set]`,
  each with its reason (64-bit wrapping add and rotate, `u64::MAX`, the `u128` literal and
  type tag).
* `Ct/CheckTest.lean` (link), `Ct/CheckTestBuild.lean` name resolution and positive controls.
* `Ct/Erase.lean` (copy) `slhdsa_leak.f.erase_eq` for every definition of `Slhdsa/Funs.lean`.
* `Ct/Arith.lean`, `Ct/Facts.lean`, `Ct/Rel.lean`, `Ct/Sim.lean`, `Ct/Heads.lean`,
  `Ct/Attr.lean` (link).
* `Ct/FactsMulti.lean` facts on mutable sub-slices of slices.
* `Ct/Tactic.lean` (copy) `ct_step`, with two more `ct_side` alternatives.
* `Ct/Sha256Core.lean`, `Ct/CompressTop.lean`, `Ct/Sha256.lean` (link) SHA-256 (the same code).
* `Ct/Sha512.lean` SHA-512.
* `Ct/ChainTop.lean` `hash::chain_blocks` (build-specific: `../lean-hw/Ct` has its own).
* `Ct/Hash.lean`, `Ct/Wots.lean`, `Ct/Xmss.lean`, `Ct/Fors.lean`, `Ct/Slh.lean`,
  `Ct/SignFacts.lean`, `Ct/Sign.lean` the relational lemmas and the simulators, generic in the
  hash length `N` and the parameter set `p` (adapted from the single-set tree's files of the same
  names).
* `Ct/Theorems.lean` SHA-256 / SHA-512 headlines and the generic key-generation statements.
* `Ct/Encoding.lean` `encoding.rs` (generic codec).
* `Ct/Sets/Sha2_*.lean` GENERATED by `scripts/gen/ct_thms.py`: per set, the
  counterparts of the single-set tree's headline statements, with `#print axioms`.
-/
